# Shell scripts must check out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Development here happens on Windows, where git's autocrlf would hand `scripts/ci.sh` a CRLF line
# ending — including on the shebang line, where `#!/usr/bin/env sh\r` names an interpreter called
# "sh\r" and the script dies with a message that does not mention line endings. Nothing in this
# repository runs those scripts today, so the failure would wait until the first Linux checkout: a
# self-hosted runner, a colleague, or a container invoking ./scripts/ci.sh instead of node directly.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Dockerfile and compose file are read by tooling that is happier with LF and never needs CRLF.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
